---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Privacy Policy" description="What HSL's Blog collects through comments and visit statistics, why, how long it is kept and how to delete it.">
  <header class="page-top"><div class="article-shell"><div class="section-kicker">Policy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>This blog has no accounts and no advertising or tracking cookies. It handles only the minimum needed for comments and visit statistics.</p></div></header>
  <div class="article-body article-shell">
    <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Comments</strong>: nickname, comment text, time posted, password (stored only as an irreversible hash), and a hashed IP value for spam control (the IP address itself is not stored)</li>
      <li><strong>Visit statistics</strong>: the article address visited and daily view counts. No cookies, IP addresses or device identifiers are stored</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>2. Why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To publish comments and confirm the author when deleting (nickname and password must match)</li>
      <li>To prevent flooding and spam</li>
      <li>To understand which articles are read and improve the blog</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>3. How long</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Comments stay until the author or the operator deletes them. Deletion is immediate; a comment with replies remains only as "deleted"</li>
      <li>Hashed IP values are erased automatically 30 days after posting</li>
      <li>Visit statistics are kept only as aggregate counts that cannot identify anyone</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. Sharing and processors</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or share this information. The blog and its database run on Cloudflare, Inc. infrastructure, so data may be processed and stored outside Korea, including in the United States.</p>
    <h2>5. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>No cookies are used. Only your theme setting and comment nickname are kept in your browser's localStorage; they are not sent to the server and you can clear them at any time.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can delete your comment at any time with the nickname and password you entered</li>
      <li>If you forgot the nickname or password, leave a comment on the same article asking for deletion and the operator will remove it</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>7. Responsible person</h2>
    <p>The blog operator, HSL, is responsible for personal information handling. Requests are handled through the method in section 6.</p>
    <h2>8. Effective date</h2>
    <p>This policy applies from September 27, 2026. Changes will be announced on this page with a new effective date.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
